The SDL OSD under BananaOS's launcher:
- quit on SDL_QUIT: SIGTERM and SIGINT (which SDL turns into SDL_QUIT) end the emulation cleanly, NVRAM and
  settings saved; MAME ignored them, so the quit combo and the shutdown could only kill it;
- SIGUSR1 opens or closes the menu (a press and release of Tab, its key): the RG DS's F, which MAME doesn't see,
  through gw-hotkeys.

